{
  "_comment": "Config matrix for tools/screenshot_matrix.py. Every config sends defaults merged with its overrides, so shots are order-independent. Symbolic names (layouts, widgets, weather conditions) are resolved by the script; colors are '#RRGGBB'. A config may also carry an 'env' object for emulator state that isn't a setting -- time ('HH:MM'), battery (percent), charging (bool) -- which is restored after the shot. Weather values of -2147483648 (INT32_MIN) put that reading back into its loading state. Configs are written for rect watches (a packed sidebar list plus bottom-bar slots) and translated for round ones: the bar's widgets go on the right arc and the sidebar's on the left, or with no bar widgets the sidebar list is split across both arcs. Configs named 'arc-*' are written for round directly (slots 0-2 left arc, 3-5 right) and sent as-is.",
